# Version control — never needed inside a build context, and .git/ can be
# large; excluding it keeps the context small and prevents any historical
# blob (including anything scrubbed from the working tree but still present
# in history) from ever entering an image layer.
.git/
.gitignore

# Environment / secrets (CLAUDE.md: all secrets via env vars only, never
# committed, never baked into an image layer). A secret must never enter a
# Docker build context — internal/config/config.go documents the process
# environment as the single source of truth at runtime, and copying .env
# into the context would risk it landing in a committed/pushed image layer.
.env
.env.*

# Go build artifacts (rebuilt inside the go-build stage; a stale host
# binary must never be trusted over what the stage compiles itself)
/bin/
/server
*.exe
*.test
*.out
coverage.out
coverage.html

# Go workspace files (local multi-module dev only; not a build input)
go.work
go.work.sum

# Frontend build output and dependency caches (rebuilt inside the
# web-build stage; trusting a host-built tree here would defeat the
# whole point of the Node stage building the SPA itself — see Dockerfile)
node_modules/
web/node_modules/
web/build/
web/.react-router/

# Committed webassets tree — deliberately excluded. The image builds the
# SPA itself (D-10), so excluding this makes a broken Node/Go build stage
# fail loudly at `go build` (missing go:embed source) rather than silently
# falling back to whatever was last committed here.
internal/webassets/build/client/

# GSD planning tool state — not a build input
.planning/

# Editor / IDE
.vscode/
.idea/

# Claude Code project state (session data, agent worktrees) — never a build input
.claude/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
